      "id": 55377,
      "name": "Ameena",
      "username": "Ameena",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-03-17T19:20:10.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I'm still unsure as to how redirection works with regard to Nemesis bonus. If someone is trying to hit someone else and a third person jumps in the way, the person performing the attack isn't going to abruptly decide to hit harder (or softer) depending on the identity of those targets, are they? So if someone is attacking their Nemesis but something else redirects it (eg Spite tries to hit Wraith but Legacy uses Lead from the Front), does the Nemesis bonus go away for the attack as it now hits a non-Nemesis. And if someone tries to hit someone but it's redirected <span class=\"bbcode-i\">to</span> a Nemesis (eg Blade tries to hit someone and Legacy intercepts via Lead from the Front), does the damage go <span class=\"bbcode-i\">up</span> even though its redirection and shouldn't be affected by the nature of the new target?</p>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:30:05.312Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 7382,
      "topic_slug": "redirect-inquiry",
      "display_username": "Ameena",
      "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
      "flair_bg_color": "",
